      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It’s posts like this and the: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1212-eac-disproportionately-punishes-deaf-and-hard-of-hearing-users \nThat make me so sad about this update. I know a lot of people are angry about quality of life mods and that’s valid but it’s the people with disabilities that are getting the worst right now. In the dev blog, they say that they want to implement quality of life features that mods already have and that will be added in “future updates”. However we all know that will take a long time for them to actually add to the game which makes me fear for the disabled communities because if the voices of the overall community aren’t being heard then the smaller communities will be utterly ignored. Let’s all pray that this update (if it does go into affect) will not be as harsh as it seems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
